    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 full suite: **42 tests, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded an optional, validated-when-present `postcode` (4 digits) to owner creation.\n\n**Contract & persistence**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added `postcode` to the `OwnerFields` schema (optional string, not in `required`), so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` gain the field and it round-trips on `GET`.\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added the `postcode` field + accessors (`@Column(name = \"postcode\")`). MapStruct maps it by name in both directions, so it's stored on create and returned on read.\n- Added a `postcode VARCHAR(4)` column to all four schemas (hsqldb \u2014 the test DB, plus h2/postgres/mysql).\n\n**Validation (OfficeFloor function pipeline, per AGENTS.md)**\n- New `RequireOwnerPostcode` step: no-ops when postcode is absent (backward-compatible); when present, requires 4 digits and \u2014 for cities with a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne\u2192VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane\u2192QLD 4000\u20134099) \u2014 enforces the range. Unknown-region cities accept any 4-digit value.\n- New checked `OwnerPostcodeInvalidException` + handler responding **400**, wired via an escalation YAML.\n- Inserted the `postcode` step into `owners.POST.yml` right after `require` (which publishes the validated body) so an out-of-range/malformed postcode fails fast as a 400 before anything is built or saved.\n\nOne bug caught during testing: `Map.of(...).get(null)` throws NPE on a null key, which hit for cities with no region \u2014 fixed by guarding the region lookup before the range map.\n\nScope note: I left the `PUT` (update) pipeline's `ApplyOwner` untouched since the spec and tests target create; updates preserve an existing postcode. Let me know if you'd like postcode to be settable on update too.",
